  "subtitle": "Dr Anouk Mensah and the sentences that outlive their reasons",
  "summary": "Postdoctoral Fellow Dr Anouk Mensah catalogues the sentences an organisation keeps saying after the reason for them has gone. In this profile she takes three of her own studies in turn: fourteen price-match promises that gained one comma between them in a decade while their fine print grew sixfold, a share house's quiet hours pinned at ten and kept past eleven, and a library desk still classed as interim after seven extensions. The narrator adds her citation record, ahead of most senior staff in the School of Emergent Priorities.",
